  "narrative": {
    "text": "Figure 2(d): the refined blueprint after the prover's second pass. Rectangles are definitions and ellipses are theorems; dashed arrows mark a statement-level use and solid arrows a proof-level use. Definition nodes taylorKernel, taylorRemainderKernel, taylorPoly, lineMap and lineCurve sit at the top; the target frechet_taylor_integral is the sink at the bottom. Nearly every lemma is dark green; three remain light blue -- taylor_remainder_by_parts, lineCurve_iteratedDeriv and frechet_taylor_integral -- which are the nodes the text says were left for a human. taylor_integral_kernel, taylor_integral_explicit and taylor_integral_one_shot are a lighter green.",
